<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-pay/">Apple Pay</a> is <a href="https://www.apple.com/in/newsroom/2026/09/apple-pay-launches-in-india/">now available in India</a>, which means customers with an eligible card can add it to the Wallet app on iPhone and Apple Watch for contactless and online payments.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/Apple-Pay-India.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1067829" /><br/>
To use <a href="https://www.apple.com/in/apple-pay/">Apple Pay in India</a>, users will need an Axis Bank credit card on the Visa or Mastercard network. Earlier today, <em>TechCrunch</em> reported that merchants and payment terminals will need to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/29/apple-pay-reportedly-launching-in-india-today/">add Apple Pay support</a>, so the service might not work at every contactless payment location.<br/>
<br/>
RuPay, India's domestic card network, is not compatible with &zwnj;Apple Pay&zwnj;. Major banks such as HDFC Bank, ICICI Bank, and SBI Card have not added support either.<br/>
<br/>
